# README maintenance

| File | Audience |
|------|----------|
| **`README.md`** | Short, fun, user-facing (no file paths or deploy plumbing) |
| **`docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`** | Dev hub: architecture, local setup, env, links to other docs |
| **`docs/FEATURES.md`** | Detailed product / route / notification / worker behavior |
| **`docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`** | Tests, CI, Heroku dynos, build pipeline |
| **`docs/OPERATIONS.md`** | **Critical operations** — cache, SW, pick timing, troubleshooting |

## When to update

Do **not** update `README.md` or `docs/*` for small code changes, especially UX tweaks (e.g., UI shapes, styling, colors, micro-copy, badge tweaks, layout spacing, minor component visual enhancements, or refactors).

Only update documentation for:
- Major new user-facing features, new leagues, new routes/pages
- Local dev environment or architecture additions (`docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`)
- CI, Heroku dyno, or build pipeline changes (`docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`)
- Critical operational behavior: cache/SW, worker contracts, notification architecture (`docs/OPERATIONS.md`)

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| Major new feature, league, tab | `README.md` + `docs/FEATURES.md` |
| Local dev, architecture, env | `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` |
| CI, Heroku, `heroku-postbuild`, tests gate | `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` |
| Critical operations (SW, worker, cache logic) | `docs/OPERATIONS.md` |

## Agent checklist

1. Small code change or UX tweak? **Do NOT update any docs.**
2. Major feature or substantial behavioral addition? Update the appropriate file using the table above.
3. Critical production behavior always lands in **`docs/OPERATIONS.md`**.

